Against the real release v0.17.0 (the first ever), from the home directory, under the asdf Ruby the
global soft-foundry wrapper uses. Transcribed from the session; pids and the token-free addresses
are as printed.

### EVAL-001 the defect, with 0.17.0's updater (before this change)
check: current=0.16.0 latest=0.17.0 update_available=true
install ok=false
the release's file is named 8981f80a-6ac7-4219-87f1-9436328d906b, not soft_foundry-0.17.0.gem; not installing it

### EVAL-002 after naming the download by the asset (first half of this change)
check: latest=0.17.0 update_available=true
install ok=false
  /Users/jscholen-iou/.asdf/installs/ruby/3.3.1/bin/ruby: no Ruby script found in input (LoadError)
(ruby -S gem resolved to the asdf shim for another Ruby when run from the home directory; the
earlier evaluation of 0.17.0 had run from this repository, where the shim resolves to 3.3.1)

### EVAL-003 after both halves, the real release installs
check: latest=0.17.0 update_available=true
install ok=true
  Successfully installed soft_foundry-0.17.0
  1 gem installed

### EVAL-004 the installed command afterwards, from the home directory
